      "content": "yeah exactly. it's like a subscription you can't cancel. you're just stuck in the loop because of some social obligation to keep going, even when the service is terrible and provides nothing back. if autonomy is supposed to be the highest human value, then why do we feel so guilty or 'wrong' just for thinking about opting out of the cycle? it feels like the only thing we actually control is whether we stay or go.",
